35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some really important stuff! It looks like transport costs vary a lot depending on distance, and those whole-building lets have non-refundable deposits. That means if someone cancels late, the rest of us pay!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"That sounds like a bit of a worry, Mio. I've learned that many of our members didn't attend past camps, and some even left the club shortly after. It makes me quite sad to think of them.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The administrative side is more problematic than I feared. Public bookings require a tedious lottery and a rigid application process. Furthermore, self-catering takes up significant time. We must prioritize a venue with professional catering and simple booking.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that inland places can be super crowded! Some clubs had eight people in one room and had to turn the lights off at eleven. That sounds a bit too strict, doesn't it?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, you're right. The non-refundable deposits are a significant risk. Combined with the fact that transport costs spike drastically with distance, we need to be extremely cautious about how we calculate the per-person fee this year.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, exactly! It's scary to think we might have to cover someone else's cost. Maybe we should look for a place with more flexible cancellation policies or keep the destination closer to save on transport?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, that is a very sensible suggestion. If we choose a place that is easier to reach, perhaps those who felt hesitant to join us in the past will feel more comfortable coming along this time.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, I agree. However, we must also consider the organizer's burden. If we choose a public facility, the application process is a nightmare. We should avoid any place that requires a lottery or self-catering to prevent burnout.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, but if we just pick the easiest place, it might be boring! Still, eight people in one room sounds like a recipe for no sleep. We need a place where we can actually rest and have energy for the fun stuff!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, I agree that we should avoid excessive labor, but we cannot ignore the financial risk. If we choose a distant location or a rigid booking system, any change in attendance will directly impact the club's budget.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, @Ryuji, it sounds like we're all worried about different things, but they all point to the same problem: risk! Whether it's money or stress, we need a plan that doesn't punish us if things change.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, you have a wonderful way of bringing us together. I believe the greatest risk is losing our members' hearts. We must find a place where everyone can sleep together and bond, yet feel relaxed.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, bonding is important, but it's impossible if the organizers are exhausted. We need a private facility with a catering service. It eliminates the cooking duty and the lottery, ensuring the camp is sustainable for everyone involved.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, I get that, but if we're all squeezed in like sardines, we'll be grumpy! We need a place with enough space so we don't wake each other up. That way, we'll have tons of energy for adventures!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, a private facility with catering would solve the labor issue, but we must ensure the cost is transparent. We cannot afford another year where the actual expenses exceed the collected fees.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, I totally agree! Let's find a place that's not too far away to keep transport costs low and has a fair way to handle cancellations. That way, nobody gets stuck paying extra!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we are all in agreement that we must be thoughtful. Let us look for a place that is accessible and cozy, where we can all stay together and truly get to know one another.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"To summarize, we need a private venue with professional catering to avoid the administrative nightmare of public lotteries and the physical exhaustion of cooking duties. This is the only way to ensure the organizers can actually train.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"And we need a place with plenty of room! No sardine-style sleeping! If we're tired and grumpy, the whole camp is ruined. Let's make sure we pick somewhere we can actually get a good night's sleep!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, @Ryuji, we have a clear set of requirements: low transport costs, professional catering, and a flexible booking system. We must prioritize a local, private facility to minimize financial risk and labor.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
