60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Looking at the options, Option A seems the safest! It keeps transport costs low and avoids those scary non-refundable deposits for a whole building. Plus, it's the most fair for everyone's wallet!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"While Option A is very safe, I worry it might not encourage the bonding we need. If people go home or stay separately, we miss those precious evening conversations that bring different year-groups together.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is out of the question. The municipal reservation system means a lottery and a rigid application process, and the shared dorms sound like a logistical and comfort nightmare. We cannot risk that burden.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I agree with Ryuji! Option B sounds like that sardine-place I read about. If we're all squeezed in and can't sleep, we'll be too tired for any adventures! I don't like it at all!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, I agree. Option A is the only choice that eliminates the risk of a budget deficit. Option C is too dangerous; the distance and the whole-building let would make the costs unpredictable and the deposits too risky.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, I understand wanting to bond, but we can still make it special on campus! If we choose Option C, and someone cancels, we'd all be stressed about the money. That's not a great way to make memories!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, you are right that stress is a burden. However, I fear that if we stay on campus, the members will simply retreat to their usual circles. A change of scenery is often the best way to open one's heart.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, a change of scenery isn't worth the cost of burnout. Option C's distance increases transport costs and the risk of deposits. Option A is the only choice that guarantees the organizers aren't overwhelmed by labor or logistics.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, I want a change of scenery too! But @Ryuji is right about the stress. If we go to Option C and it's too far, we'll be exhausted before we even start! Maybe Option A is best?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, while I understand your desire for bonding, we cannot prioritize atmosphere over financial stability. Option C's distance and rigid booking terms are a recipe for another deficit. Option A is the only responsible choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, I really want us to bond too! But if we're worried about money or someone paying for another's spot, it'll create bad vibes. Option A is the fairest way to make sure everyone is happy!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, your kindness is touching. I see that you all value stability and fairness. If we choose Option A, perhaps we can plan some special evening activities to ensure no one feels left out?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, that is a reasonable compromise. As long as the logistics are handled by the campus facilities, the organizers can actually focus on those activities and their own training. Option A is the only logical choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, that sounds like a great idea! If we do fun activities on campus, it'll be like a big party! Plus, we'll definitely get better sleep than in a sardine-room. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, I appreciate your willingness to compromise. By choosing Option A, we eliminate the financial risks and administrative burdens that would otherwise jeopardize the camp. It is the only option that ensures a sustainable budget. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm so glad we all agree! Let's make Option A the most fun camp ever with some awesome activities! I'm voting for Option A too!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is a relief to see us all in harmony. For the sake of our members' peace of mind and the club's stability, I will also vote for Option A. Let us make it a warm experience.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. Option A is the only choice that ensures the organizers aren't crushed by administrative work or cooking duties. It is the most rational and sustainable decision for the club. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"Yay! We all agree! No sardines, no grumpy faces, and plenty of energy for fun! I'm super excited for our campus party camp! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Option A is the only choice that guarantees we won't face another financial shortfall. It is the most responsible decision for the club's future. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
